1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:23,333
I'll be right back.

3
00:01:34,552 --> 00:01:37,430
I'll bring your brother out. Hmm?

4
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:39,450
EPISODE 2

5
00:02:39,951 --> 00:02:42,912
The press release about the surgery
is scheduled to come out today.

6
00:02:44,581 --> 00:02:45,415
And sir,

7
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:48,418
we were also able to expand
the pediatric cancer ward

8
00:02:48,501 --> 00:02:50,336
thanks to his contribution.

9
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:53,548
However, our hospital
is the only one that is unprofitable.

10
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:54,966
But he's sick.

11
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:56,968
And in more ways than one.

12
00:02:57,844 --> 00:03:00,346
So even though the net profit
of the foundation's hospital

13
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:01,764
is in the tens of billions,

14
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:03,558
we still have to cater to VIP donors?

15
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:07,604
The staff room expansion
has been put on hold,

16
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:09,856
and there's still no answer
from the foundation.

17
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:13,568
Please compile a list
of all hospital donations.

18
00:03:13,651 --> 00:03:15,778
Dr. Do, why are we performing surgery,

19
00:03:15,862 --> 00:03:18,406
without trying preemptive
chemotherapy first?

20
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,868
Well sir, i-it was the patient's demand.

21
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:23,870
There's no changing his mind.

22
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:26,789
He says that right now
he needs to keep his wits about him.

23
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:28,917
And from what's going on outside,
I can see why.

24
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,793
WAGE WITHHOLDING, MISMANAGEMENT,
AND ABUSE OF POWER

25
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:32,170
He's arrived at the hospital.

26
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:34,047
Dr. Ma Seong-gyu is downstairs.

27
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:35,215
Dr. Do.

28
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:38,968
Do you think you're up to it?

29
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:48,937
MONTHLY RENTALS AVAILABLE

30
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:50,104
1.5 MILLION PER MONTH (NEGOTIABLE)

31
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:51,689
"A hundred fifty per month."

32
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:54,609
Way too expensive.

33
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:02,200
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

34
00:04:07,163 --> 00:04:09,374
Park Gwang-cheol must resign!

35
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:11,793
Resign! Resign!

36
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:13,378
Pay your workers what you owe!

37
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:15,797
Pay us! Pay us!

38
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,590
Park Gwang-cheol must step down!

39
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:19,759
Step down! Step down!

40
00:04:19,842 --> 00:04:21,886
Pay your workers what you owe!

41
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:24,138
Pay us! Pay us!

42
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:32,397
Are you a person who's sick,
or are you visiting someone?

43
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:35,942
- That's okay.
- Oh, it's all right. It's my gift to you.

44
00:04:36,025 --> 00:04:37,318
So eat up, okay?

45
00:04:45,743 --> 00:04:49,080
I could take it off your hands
if she doesn't want that.

46
00:04:51,499 --> 00:04:52,500
Thank you.

47
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:01,384
Hey, here he comes!

48
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:08,349
Hey! Pay us, greedy pigs!

49
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:13,229
Hey! I see you! Pay us!

50
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:18,026
What makes you so much better than us?

51
00:05:18,109 --> 00:05:19,235
Hey! We're patients too.

52
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:20,737
Look, he's going inside.

53
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:23,156
- You need to stay out here.
- Why does he get to go in ahead of us?

54
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:24,657
We're patients!

55
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:27,160
Let me ask you something.

56
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:28,911
A-All right.

57
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:31,414
Is it true that I'm actually sick?

58
00:05:31,497 --> 00:05:33,624
The cancer diagnosis was legitimate?

59
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:34,917
Yes, I'm afraid so, sir.

60
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:37,462
Nobody believes it's true.

61
00:05:37,545 --> 00:05:40,923
I lied about being sick to avoid
the National Assembly audit.

62
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:44,510
I pretended to collapse
in order to delay my trial,

63
00:05:45,094 --> 00:05:48,097
and now that I really am sick

64
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:51,768
these folks decided to come down here
just to raise hell outside.

65
00:05:51,851 --> 00:05:53,978
Well, stress can exacerbate your symptoms.

66
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:56,022
Dr. Do is a fantastic surgeon,

67
00:05:56,105 --> 00:05:57,815
and he's extremely knowledgeable.

68
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:59,359
Rest assured, you're in great hands.

69
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:01,652
You've got a bright future here.

70
00:06:03,863 --> 00:06:06,199
Thank you, sir. My name is Ma Seong-gyu.

71
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:08,826
Before we go to my room,

72
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:11,454
let's go see
that pediatric cancer ward I financed.

73
00:06:11,996 --> 00:06:14,374
I couldn't show my face back then
because of the trial.

74
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:16,793
I heard you put my name up on a plaque.

75
00:06:17,502 --> 00:06:19,545
Yes, we certainly did.

76
00:06:23,257 --> 00:06:25,760
<i>This is the story of a lone wolf.</i>

77
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:27,929
Hey, Gye Su-jeong.

78
00:06:28,012 --> 00:06:29,013
I need to borrow this.

79
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:33,184
<i>A solitary figure who emerged</i>
<i>in the era of the mafia in white,</i>

80
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:38,439
<i>an age in which the practice of medicine,</i>
<i>where life and death hang in the balance…</i>

81
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:41,609
- This is an emergency!
<i>- …is driven by money and power.</i>

82
00:06:41,692 --> 00:06:43,236
<i>- She belongs to no group.</i>
- She took my chair!

83
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:45,613
<i>- She is unaffiliated with any department.</i>
- Gye Su-jeong!

84
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:47,657
<i>- This woman, right here…</i>
- Gye Su-jeong!

85
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:55,832
- Come back here! Gye Su-jeong!
<i>- She despises authority</i>

86
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:57,917
<i>- and answers to no one.</i>
- Hey, wait!

87
00:06:58,501 --> 00:07:01,170
<i>Her only weapons are her medical license</i>

88
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:04,090
<i>and the surgical skills</i>
<i>she honed from the ground up.</i>

89
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:13,808
No pneumothorax. Can you hear me?
Can you tell me your name?

90
00:07:13,891 --> 00:07:15,226
Lee Ju-hui.

91
00:07:15,852 --> 00:07:17,019
Juvenile diabetes.

92
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:23,151
- Check her EMR stat.
- Okay. I'm on it.

93
00:07:26,112 --> 00:07:27,530
Well, this is embarrassing.

94
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:29,866
Who was that crazy girl?

95
00:07:34,412 --> 00:07:37,039
<i>Gye Su-jeong, general surgeon.</i>

96
00:07:37,123 --> 00:07:38,541
<i>Also known as</i>…

97
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:41,294
<i>Doctor X.</i>

98
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:46,674
<i>Chairman Park Gwang-cheol…</i>

99
00:07:46,757 --> 00:07:48,426
Seriously, this is just…

100
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:51,637
…<i>to avoid serving of his sentence.</i>

101
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,139
Are we seriously working with her?

102
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:54,849
We have to.

103
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:57,268
It was Director Bu's decision

104
00:07:57,351 --> 00:07:58,478
and we are short on doctors.

105
00:07:58,561 --> 00:08:01,522
But she does whatever she wants.
It's completely ridiculous.

106
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:06,068
- Yeah, but it was an emergency.
- I know, but…

107
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:09,238
now everyone I know
is gonna see me on the news.

108
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:11,657
Don't worry, you look amazing on camera.

109
00:08:11,741 --> 00:08:13,576
Oh, don't say that.

110
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:15,203
You did good.

111
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:19,040
You want revenge?

112
00:08:20,416 --> 00:08:22,293
Let's go distract her,
that way she can't focus.

113
00:08:22,376 --> 00:08:23,794
Okay. Okay.

114
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:27,215
Well…

115
00:08:31,302 --> 00:08:32,428
Hey.

116
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:34,222
- Uh, want some coffee?
- Yeah, coffee.

117
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:35,640
Yeah, mmm, coffee.

118
00:08:41,812 --> 00:08:43,856
Excuse me, excuse me. Earbuds.

119
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:46,859
Oh, man.

120
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:50,321
Oh, yeah.

121
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:53,866
You should assist Dr. Do
with his surgery, okay?

122
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:55,034
I thought you were gonna do it.

123
00:08:55,117 --> 00:08:57,036
No, I can't be the one to assist.

124
00:08:57,578 --> 00:09:01,666
He'd know right away that I was only there
because I don't trust his surgical skills.

125
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:04,252
Someone at your level should assist,
so he doesn't get suspicious.

126
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:07,129
Okay. But, um, how did Dr. Do end up--

127
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:08,506
It was decided over drinks.

128
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:12,760
It seems Dr. Do kept filling
Chairman Park's glass that day,

129
00:09:12,843 --> 00:09:15,888
and he was in such a good mood
that he appointed him primary surgeon.

130
00:09:16,472 --> 00:09:18,266
Who picks their surgeon on a whim though?

131
00:09:18,349 --> 00:09:20,309
Well, because everybody wanted to do it,

132
00:09:20,393 --> 00:09:22,853
and he decided to choose
the one who'd walk on eggshells

133
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:26,274
and grovel at his feet the most
out of all the hospital's surgeons.

134
00:09:26,357 --> 00:09:28,401
And Dr. Do simply couldn't refuse.

135
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:30,778
- Oh, wow.
- That's garbage.

136
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:36,826
Is it?

137
00:09:46,210 --> 00:09:48,713
Don't make eye contact with her.
Don't make eye contact.

138
00:09:48,796 --> 00:09:49,797
Yeah, okay.

139
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:52,508
- I'm not looking at her. I'm not looking.
- Neither am I.

140
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:54,552
We'll lose if we do.

141
00:09:57,054 --> 00:09:59,515
The staff room used to be
my home away from home

142
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,642
and now I feel so uncomfortable here.

143
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:05,438
That privacy screen over there
could be helpful in this situation.

144
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:07,648
- Yeah, good idea.
- Let's set it up.

145
00:10:07,732 --> 00:10:08,983
Okay, let's do it.

146
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:20,995
Now I'm anxious because I can't see her.

147
00:10:21,078 --> 00:10:22,413
I can't tell what she's up to.

148
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:23,706
- Put it away?
- I think we'd better.

149
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:25,583
- Let's put it away. Sorry.
- I'm a little scared.

150
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:26,709
Lift.

151
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:29,837
There we go. There we go.

152
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:37,762
I'm uncomfortable again
now that I can see her.

153
00:10:38,512 --> 00:10:41,182
I'm uncomfortable when I can see her,
and anxious when I can't.

154
00:10:41,265 --> 00:10:42,266
She's so annoying.

155
00:10:44,602 --> 00:10:46,145
Oh, Dr. Do. Hello.

156
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:54,945
Those go over there.

157
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:56,781
W-What?

158
00:10:56,864 --> 00:10:58,491
Oh, yes, sir.

159
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:08,834
Dr. Gye, nice to see you again.

160
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:11,545
Hey, who told you to put them there?

161
00:11:11,629 --> 00:11:13,714
This is a walkway here.
They don't go there.

162
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:17,093
- What?
- You need to put them on the desk.

163
00:11:17,176 --> 00:11:20,388
Oh, uh, yeah.
But this is Dr. Gye Su-jeong's desk…

164
00:11:20,471 --> 00:11:21,597
Let's do this, intern.

165
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:26,852
There we go.

166
00:11:27,853 --> 00:11:29,814
There we go.

167
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:40,157
- What's this?
- My terms of employment.

168
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:43,327
"Accompanying director rounds, attending
rounds, and attending company dinners."

169
00:11:43,411 --> 00:11:44,745
That is not something I do.

170
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:47,164
"Ghostwriting papers and compiling
research materials for attendings."

171
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:48,499
That is not something I do.

172
00:11:50,751 --> 00:11:51,794
I know, I heard.

173
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:55,297
I didn't bring these in here
so you could draft me a paper.

174
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:57,341
I just picked out some materials
that might help.

175
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:59,009
You can read them at your leisure.

176
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:00,553
Only…

177
00:12:03,347 --> 00:12:05,599
there's just no room for them
anywhere else.

178
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:09,562
Our staff room is so very small.

179
00:12:10,312 --> 00:12:14,233
Uh, well, we could split them up
and put some on my desk.

180
00:12:14,316 --> 00:12:16,652
- That'll free up some space for Dr. Gye.
- Hey, Park Tae-gyeong.

181
00:12:18,529 --> 00:12:20,865
- Hey, Park Tae-gyeong. Park Tae-gyeong.
- Dr. Gye?

182
00:12:20,948 --> 00:12:23,242
Boy, I don't know if there's
anywhere else she can go.

183
00:12:23,325 --> 00:12:26,078
- Nice.
- Dr. Tae-gyeong. How's it going?

184
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:29,790
From now on, your job is
to be Dr. Gye's surveillance camera.

185
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:30,875
What?

186
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:32,668
I want you to keep an eye on her.

187
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:34,920
Uh, well, I'm an intern.

188
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:36,255
I have to do my studies.

189
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:40,092
I managed to get all my studying done
while juggling multiple attendings.

190
00:12:40,176 --> 00:12:41,594
You just have to watch one mad dog.

191
00:12:41,677 --> 00:12:43,345
- "Mad dog"?
- Yeah.

192
00:12:43,429 --> 00:12:45,681
Yeah. We all call her mad dog.

193
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:47,975
Because she's crazy as a rabid dog.

194
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:49,185
So now it's her nickname.

195
00:12:49,268 --> 00:12:50,644
But isn't that a little childish?

196
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:52,021
Mocking someone just because

197
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:53,856
you don't understand them?

198
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:56,233
I mean, it's exactly
what bullies do on a playground.

199
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:59,695
- Hey, I'm not some kind of bully.
- Okay, the surveillance camera is now on.

200
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:21,842
Here we go.

201
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:25,012
Dr. Gye, I've been looking for you.

202
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:28,641
Are you working here?
Why don't we go in then?

203
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:31,602
Oh, you left your bag behind, huh?

204
00:13:31,685 --> 00:13:33,729
Well, I've got my wallet. I'll get this…

205
00:13:38,609 --> 00:13:41,862
One strawberry cake,
one Earl Grey pound cake, one croffle set,

206
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:43,823
and a large vanilla latte, extra sweet.

207
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:47,618
Go get her.
Bring that mad dog here right now.

208
00:13:47,701 --> 00:13:51,205
She may have overreacted a little, uh,
in the heat of the moment.

209
00:13:52,373 --> 00:13:56,335
Hey. Mr. New-Director, listen up.

210
00:13:56,418 --> 00:13:58,754
If I die, there will be a lot of people
whose lives will…

211
00:13:58,838 --> 00:14:00,840
Oh, sir. I'm sure they'll be
so sad and devastated.

212
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:02,591
…be easier.

213
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:05,386
They'll all be glad.
They'll say everything was my fault.

214
00:14:06,303 --> 00:14:09,557
They'll dump all the shit
they created right into my tomb.

215
00:14:10,474 --> 00:14:11,350
Dying…

216
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:14,311
is not an option.

217
00:14:14,895 --> 00:14:17,439
You have to save my life, no matter what.
Got it?

218
00:14:19,024 --> 00:14:20,359
Well, answer me!

219
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:22,236
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

220
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:26,907
Ah, I'm glad you have a healthy appetite.

221
00:14:26,991 --> 00:14:29,243
Oh, Dr. Gye, maybe I should get your bag.

222
00:14:30,452 --> 00:14:32,538
You had your wallet? Then why didn't you…

223
00:14:32,621 --> 00:14:35,207
- I'm broke.
- You have no money?

224
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:43,465
"Terms of employment.
Absolutely no personal conversations"?

225
00:14:47,219 --> 00:14:49,221
What if I order an extra slice
of blueberry cake--

226
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:50,890
I spent my allowance.

227
00:14:50,973 --> 00:14:53,142
All right, so you're getting an allowance.
Who from?

228
00:14:53,225 --> 00:14:54,476
- Ms. Jang.
- I see.

229
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:57,146
So she manages your money for you.
Do you live with her?

230
00:14:57,229 --> 00:14:59,773
I mean, you're a doctor.
You can't be getting a kid's allowance.

231
00:14:59,857 --> 00:15:00,941
How much money do you get?

232
00:15:06,071 --> 00:15:07,281
A hundred thousand won…

233
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:09,283
Well, that would be plenty
of money per day to--

234
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:10,618
- …per month.
- What?

235
00:15:10,701 --> 00:15:12,661
You can't be expected to live on that.

236
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:13,871
Is she blackmailing you?

237
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:22,922
I'm in debt.

238
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:25,090
What? Uh, deep in debt?

239
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:27,468
Mmm. I get in trouble if I waste it.

240
00:15:27,551 --> 00:15:28,677
Oh.

241
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:31,263
W-What do you mean you get in trouble?
Does she, like, hit you?

242
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:33,390
Mmm. She sure does.

243
00:15:33,474 --> 00:15:35,601
She hit me yesterday
for using up my allowance.

244
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:38,979
Did Ms. Jang by any chance
take your passport

245
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:40,147
or identification card?

246
00:15:41,065 --> 00:15:43,233
Mmm. Ms. Jang manages everything.

247
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:56,121
Su-jeong likes to eat her cake.

248
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:59,041
Su-jeong, you want a little cake?

249
00:15:59,124 --> 00:16:00,084
Cake!

250
00:16:00,167 --> 00:16:04,338
If you want cake, go to work
and earn some money, doctor-slave.

251
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:05,756
Put your hands up!

252
00:16:08,717 --> 00:16:10,552
I want you to sign this.

253
00:16:10,636 --> 00:16:13,806
I took out a loan under your name.

254
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:24,358
- I wanna eat more of this.
- Yeah, yeah. Please, have another.

255
00:16:24,441 --> 00:16:26,527
Uh, feel free to order
as many as you want.

256
00:16:27,236 --> 00:16:29,738
I'm buying. Go ahead and eat up.

257
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:31,782
You're a good person.

258
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:34,284
I wanna finish all this.

259
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:36,704
Have you been craving
anything in particular?

260
00:16:37,329 --> 00:16:38,372
<i>- Jjajangmyeon.</i>
- Hmm.

261
00:16:38,455 --> 00:16:40,499
- Next time I'll take you out to dinner.
- Let's do it today.

262
00:16:40,582 --> 00:16:42,167
When do you get off work?
I'm done at 6:00.

263
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:43,502
Oh, I don't get off that early.

264
00:16:44,128 --> 00:16:45,170
Just clock out at 6:00.

265
00:16:56,348 --> 00:16:58,851
<i>- Please insert your card.</i>
- Ah, those probably aren't easy to use

266
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:01,186
for the patients or the elderly,
even with someone to assist.

267
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,563
- Excuse me.
- I tried it earlier.

268
00:17:02,646 --> 00:17:04,231
I'm young, and even I had trouble with it.

269
00:17:04,314 --> 00:17:06,233
It's hard to read, and you get nervous…

270
00:17:06,316 --> 00:17:08,068
And you're aware
of all the people behind you.

271
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:11,238
- Right. That made me freeze up even more.
- Excuse me, sorry.

272
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:13,949
I felt like such a loser.
I was like, "Can I even do this?"

273
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:15,951
Can I help you with that?

274
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:17,161
Oh, yes, please.

275
00:17:17,786 --> 00:17:18,871
Oh, thanks for your help.

276
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:21,915
- At least it benefits the patients, right?
<i>- Please insert your card.</i>

277
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:23,625
It benefits the hospital.

278
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:26,211
Does it look like
it benefits the patients?

279
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:30,924
Oh, I didn't think that
you considered people like that.

280
00:17:34,136 --> 00:17:37,139
Uh, don't let it get to you,
what happened in the staff room earlier.

281
00:17:37,222 --> 00:17:38,223
What?

282
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:40,267
You know, getting kicked out
by the others.

283
00:17:40,350 --> 00:17:41,602
Rejected.

284
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:45,522
Oh… I had no idea.

285
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:50,486
Maybe you just need to lay low
for a little while, you know?

286
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:57,826
<i>Unnie!</i>

287
00:17:57,910 --> 00:18:00,454
- Hey, I could've done that.
- Oh. There you are.

288
00:18:00,537 --> 00:18:02,998
I'm just trying
to use the kiosk right now.

289
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:05,000
Oh, how's Ju-hui doing?

290
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:06,960
- Well, the pain is gone, so…
- Good.

291
00:18:07,044 --> 00:18:08,670
- She's mad though.
- Wait, what is she mad about?

292
00:18:09,421 --> 00:18:10,380
Wouldn't you be?

293
00:18:10,881 --> 00:18:13,092
She's only a kid,
and for her whole life she's been sick.

294
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:15,677
- And now it's cancer.
<i>- Please insert your card.</i>

295
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:17,221
- May I have your card?
- Oh.

296
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:21,183
They need an interim payment.

297
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:23,393
What, do they think we'll skip town
without paying?

298
00:18:24,561 --> 00:18:26,188
Hold on, wait. Wait.

299
00:18:26,271 --> 00:18:29,650
Hey. What's that? What's with that vest?

300
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:32,361
Go, get that thing outta here.
Go on, do it.

301
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:33,445
Yes sir.

302
00:18:33,529 --> 00:18:34,988
- Isn't that amazing?
- You can't be in here.

303
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:36,198
- Come on.
- What are you doing?

304
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:37,783
What's going on?
Why are you people doing this?

305
00:18:37,866 --> 00:18:39,827
- I said, let go!
- That's right.

306
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:41,954
- Oh, are you scared?
- Yeong-ju.

307
00:18:42,037 --> 00:18:43,413
Is that why you're doing this?

308
00:18:45,165 --> 00:18:46,625
What the hell are you doing?

309
00:18:46,708 --> 00:18:48,961
- Hey, that's mine!
- We didn't come to the hospital

310
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:51,130
to protest.
My daughter's a patient here, sir.

311
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:52,548
- What are you doing?
- Yeong-ju!

312
00:18:52,631 --> 00:18:54,716
- Don't push her wheelchair!
- Yeong-ju!

313
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,301
It's true, my daughter is a patient.

314
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:58,512
- We're here to visit her.
- Let go first, then we can talk.

315
00:18:58,595 --> 00:19:01,098
- I'm here for my family.
- Hey, hey. That lunatic. Why, that…

316
00:19:01,181 --> 00:19:02,141
Why didn't you get rid of her?

317
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:04,309
- You said you'd take care of it!
- I came here to be with my niece

318
00:19:04,393 --> 00:19:05,519
- and sister!
- Hey, come on…

319
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:07,354
- Yeong-ju…
- Um, excuse me!

320
00:19:07,437 --> 00:19:11,108
- It says this card's been maxed out.
- Oh, the card, the card. My card.

321
00:19:11,191 --> 00:19:13,610
The vest, my wallet's in that vest.
Could you give it to her?

322
00:19:15,070 --> 00:19:17,698
I said let go! Are you crazy?

323
00:19:17,781 --> 00:19:19,783
- Hey, hey…
- Seriously, why are you doing this?

324
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:22,578
- Let go! I said let go!
- First let go, then we can talk.

325
00:19:22,661 --> 00:19:24,746
- This is ridiculous!
- We could work this all out,

326
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:26,748
- if you let go of her!
- What is your problem?

327
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:29,168
People with nothing
are always the loudest.

328
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:31,503
They're all such pathetic losers.

329
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:35,215
- Uh, Chairman--
- Pathetic losers? Pathetic losers?

330
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:37,509
- And whose fault do you think all this is?
- Hey.

331
00:19:37,593 --> 00:19:39,469
Give my aunt her pay!

332
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:41,054
- I said give it to her!
- Ju-hui!

333
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:43,473
- Ju-hui!
- Give my aunt her pay!

334
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:44,600
Ju-hui, stop it!

335
00:19:44,683 --> 00:19:47,019
Oh, gosh. Ju-hui! Ju-hui!

336
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:48,604
Ju-hui!

337
00:19:48,687 --> 00:19:50,898
- Ju-hui, hold on, I'm coming!
- Get this girl off of me!

338
00:19:50,981 --> 00:19:53,442
- What do you think you're doing?
- Ju-hui! Calm down!

339
00:19:53,525 --> 00:19:56,111
- Come on, let her go!
- Hey, let go of my daughter!

340
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:59,072
- I'll get you out of here, Chairman.
- You're going to get hurt. No

341
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:01,116
Let go. You'll get hurt.

342
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:04,161
Hey, hold on now, stop that! Ju-hui!

343
00:20:07,247 --> 00:20:08,957
What do you think you're doing?

344
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:11,084
Oh, my gosh.

345
00:20:11,168 --> 00:20:13,754
- She's bleeding. Help her!
- Let me see.

346
00:20:14,838 --> 00:20:17,257
Let go of me. I said let go of me.

347
00:20:18,091 --> 00:20:19,134
Ju-hui.

348
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:22,596
- Ju-hui.
- Unbelievable.

349
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:24,473
Are you okay?

350
00:20:27,517 --> 00:20:29,728
- Ju-hui, are you okay?
- Where'd he go?

351
00:20:29,811 --> 00:20:31,688
- Ju-hui. Hey!
- Hey, where did Chairman Park go?

352
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:33,357
- Ju-hui. Ju-hui.
- Hey, you're bleeding.

353
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:45,702
It's true…

354
00:20:46,662 --> 00:20:48,538
We really are pathetic losers.

355
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:50,332
Hey.

356
00:20:50,958 --> 00:20:52,084
Lee Ju-hui.

357
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:53,252
Lee Ju-hui!

358
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:57,673
Ju-hui. Ju-hui.

359
00:20:58,632 --> 00:21:00,008
- Ju-hui.
- What's that?

360
00:21:00,509 --> 00:21:01,718
Is that blood on the floor?

361
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:02,803
You had me worried.

362
00:21:03,595 --> 00:21:06,056
You're back already?
Where's Chairman Park?

363
00:21:06,598 --> 00:21:07,599
I parked him.

364
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:14,564
Hey!

365
00:21:15,399 --> 00:21:19,152
Hey!

366
00:21:26,868 --> 00:21:29,579
Mmm. She'll be here soon, your sister.
She's in a brief meeting

367
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:31,873
- with the hospital staff.
- Okay.

368
00:21:31,957 --> 00:21:34,668
- When she comes, you can go.
- Huh? Why?

369
00:21:34,751 --> 00:21:37,045
I'm your mother, I'm staying right here.

370
00:21:37,129 --> 00:21:38,672
<i>Two balls and one strike.</i>

371
00:21:38,755 --> 00:21:40,173
<i>Here's the fourth pitch.</i>

372
00:21:40,257 --> 00:21:42,718
<i>And it's right down the middle, strike!</i>

373
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:45,304
<i>The count is 2-2. Man.</i>

374
00:21:45,387 --> 00:21:47,806
Would you mind
stepping outside with me for a second?

375
00:21:47,889 --> 00:21:50,058
I'd like to discuss
your daughter's surgery with you.

376
00:21:50,726 --> 00:21:51,893
Okay.

377
00:21:51,977 --> 00:21:53,979
Can you wait until my aunt gets here?

378
00:21:56,898 --> 00:21:59,151
Oh, let me get you something, Doctor.

379
00:22:03,155 --> 00:22:05,782
- Here you go.
- Oh. Thanks very much.

380
00:22:07,784 --> 00:22:08,827
Dr. Gye.

381
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:27,971
Juvenile diabetes and pancreatoblastoma.

382
00:22:28,055 --> 00:22:29,056
It's a very rare case.

383
00:22:29,139 --> 00:22:31,516
Really? What's the prognosis?

384
00:22:32,517 --> 00:22:34,853
- It's hopeless.
- A lost cause?

385
00:22:34,936 --> 00:22:37,105
How could he miss that?
The game's hopeless.

386
00:22:39,983 --> 00:22:41,902
You're really one of a kind, you know?

387
00:22:45,197 --> 00:22:46,615
Excuse me.

388
00:22:48,658 --> 00:22:51,787
<i>Back-to-back hits…</i>

389
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:57,334
- Hmm.
- Where are you going?

390
00:22:58,627 --> 00:22:59,628
Dr. Gye!

391
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:02,381
W-What about Dr. Gye? What happened?

392
00:23:02,464 --> 00:23:04,341
- She disappeared.
- Disappeared?

393
00:23:04,424 --> 00:23:06,551
Where to?

394
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:11,681
Yes, Doctor. Uh, Dr. Gye should be…

395
00:23:12,641 --> 00:23:14,810
Sorry? What incident?

396
00:23:15,310 --> 00:23:17,062
No, when did…

397
00:23:18,271 --> 00:23:20,273
She disappeared a minute ago.

398
00:23:32,494 --> 00:23:35,455
- Uh, Dr. Gye. So, uh…
- Where's Dr. Gye? Show your face.

399
00:23:35,539 --> 00:23:38,041
- Hmm? I know you're here.
- Isn't that her?

400
00:23:38,125 --> 00:23:39,584
Yeah, there she is.

401
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:42,379
Oh, this is her. Right?

402
00:23:42,462 --> 00:23:43,880
- That's her.
- She can really put it away.

403
00:23:43,964 --> 00:23:45,173
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

404
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:49,719
- Dr. Gye!
- What are you doing?

405
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:51,221
What's going on?

406
00:23:51,304 --> 00:23:52,472
Uh, Dr. Gye.

407
00:23:52,973 --> 00:23:55,684
What were you doing before
we met at the coffee shop earlier?

408
00:24:00,063 --> 00:24:02,149
- I was in the hallway.
- What were you doing in the hallway?

409
00:24:02,232 --> 00:24:04,109
I saw a patient
lying there with dizziness,

410
00:24:04,192 --> 00:24:06,903
so I asked her a few questions
and sent her to the ENT.

411
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:07,821
She had Ménière's.

412
00:24:07,904 --> 00:24:11,450
You're telling me that a temp like you
diagnosed Ménière's disease, huh?

413
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:13,285
Would you keep it down, please?

414
00:24:13,368 --> 00:24:15,245
Is that really what you're all
up in arms about?

415
00:24:15,328 --> 00:24:18,039
That patient was waiting
to be seen by Internal Medicine

416
00:24:18,123 --> 00:24:20,959
and now she's over in ENT,
lying on a couch.

417
00:24:21,918 --> 00:24:23,587
- What about the tests?
- We did them.

418
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:27,215
She's unable to hear low frequencies
and she's got nystagmus.

419
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:29,551
- It's Ménière's.
- No issue then.

420
00:24:29,634 --> 00:24:31,678
No, that's not the only issue here.

421
00:24:31,761 --> 00:24:34,890
She crossed the line and interfered
in another department's patient care.

422
00:24:35,932 --> 00:24:38,852
She'd spent years going from one local
clinic to another in the countryside,

423
00:24:38,935 --> 00:24:42,022
getting put on IVs and medication
as she grew weaker.

424
00:24:42,105 --> 00:24:44,733
Her kid finally brought her in
to a major hospital.

425
00:24:45,275 --> 00:24:46,943
No need to put her through the wringer.

426
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:48,945
Even her own kid chalked it up
to geriatric depression

427
00:24:49,029 --> 00:24:50,780
and disregarded her symptoms.

428
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:54,159
Indeed. That's why she grabbed me
and cried on my shoulder.

429
00:24:54,242 --> 00:24:56,578
It was the first time
she'd been correctly diagnosed,

430
00:24:56,661 --> 00:24:57,871
and she was so grateful.

431
00:24:57,954 --> 00:24:59,873
And I was so embarrassed.

432
00:24:59,956 --> 00:25:02,375
By the way, did she just give us an order?

433
00:25:02,459 --> 00:25:04,002
- Mmm.
- Yes.

434
00:25:04,085 --> 00:25:06,421
So the rumors are true,
you really are disrespectful.

435
00:25:06,922 --> 00:25:08,006
Fascinating.

436
00:25:08,089 --> 00:25:10,926
Since when does a scalpel jockey
know how to diagnose patients?

437
00:25:11,009 --> 00:25:14,513
Are you saying us scalpel jockeys
can't come up with a diagnosis on our own?

438
00:25:14,596 --> 00:25:16,473
- You're completely out of line.
- Well, now…

439
00:25:16,973 --> 00:25:20,393
Well, suppose I told one of your patients
not to have surgery. How would you feel?

440
00:25:20,477 --> 00:25:23,438
Let's calm down. It's not a fight between
Internal Medicine and General Surgery.

441
00:25:23,522 --> 00:25:26,900
The problem is that Dr. Gye over here
overstepped her boundaries.

442
00:25:26,983 --> 00:25:28,276
I think we should just focus on…

443
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,695
- Hey, uh, just apologize to them already.
- …making sure that…

444
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:32,364
Oh, no need to apologize to me.

445
00:25:32,447 --> 00:25:33,657
I just came to put a face to the name

446
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:35,784
and observe the infamous snake Su-jeong.

447
00:25:36,868 --> 00:25:39,120
Don't be a stranger, huh?

448
00:25:40,038 --> 00:25:41,373
How intriguing.

449
00:25:41,456 --> 00:25:42,332
I'm leaving.

450
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:44,459
Oh, a-an apology isn't enough for me.

451
00:25:44,543 --> 00:25:47,003
She needs to face disciplinary action
or a pay cut.

452
00:25:47,504 --> 00:25:50,340
Neither would apply to me, actually.
I'm just a temp.

453
00:25:50,423 --> 00:25:52,592
How dare you keep talking back to me!

454
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:54,135
Well, she's talking back, all right.

455
00:25:54,219 --> 00:25:56,513
But she did make a good point, didn't she?

456
00:25:56,596 --> 00:25:59,349
Okay, so for now, why don't you just go?

457
00:25:59,432 --> 00:26:02,269
Let us deal with this internally
and we'll tell you what we decide. Okay?

458
00:26:02,352 --> 00:26:03,603
Deal with it properly.

459
00:26:04,271 --> 00:26:05,522
I'm not gonna just forget about it.

460
00:26:05,605 --> 00:26:06,982
Yeah, okay.

461
00:26:07,065 --> 00:26:08,441
Goodbye, Dr.

462
00:26:08,525 --> 00:26:10,318
That guy's so loud.

463
00:26:10,902 --> 00:26:14,322
He's known for his temper, now I see why.
He must pop antacids like candy.

464
00:26:14,406 --> 00:26:15,490
What do you think you're doing

465
00:26:15,574 --> 00:26:17,951
diagnosing patients who aren't yours
in the hallway?

466
00:26:18,910 --> 00:26:19,911
Donkkaseu.

467
00:26:21,079 --> 00:26:23,164
How many more helpings am I allowed?
It's good.

468
00:26:23,248 --> 00:26:25,208
- What?
- I think you should read the room…

469
00:26:25,292 --> 00:26:27,127
It's hard to find really good donkkaseu.

470
00:26:27,210 --> 00:26:31,381
- Uh, I'll get you some more later. Just…
- I'm not… Wait, hey, y- you…

471
00:26:31,464 --> 00:26:33,717
Hey, Park Tae-gyeong, what were you doing?

472
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:37,137
Oh, I apologize. I didn't think
she'd get in trouble so fast.

473
00:26:37,762 --> 00:26:39,973
Although, I'm not sure
that what she did was terrible.

474
00:26:40,056 --> 00:26:42,684
- She was just trying to help a lady who--
- You're right. She was only helping.

475
00:26:42,767 --> 00:26:44,311
But she overstepped her boundaries.

476
00:26:45,061 --> 00:26:47,397
- And she planned the whole thing.
- She did what?

477
00:26:47,981 --> 00:26:49,441
She's trying to get back in the staff room

478
00:26:49,524 --> 00:26:52,152
by making trouble
until we give her desk back to her.

479
00:26:52,944 --> 00:26:55,071
Don't tell me you got rid of
that poor woman's desk.

480
00:26:55,572 --> 00:26:57,699
That's such a horrible thing to do.

481
00:26:57,782 --> 00:26:58,825
You're absolutely right.

482
00:26:58,908 --> 00:27:02,078
I think we may have been
totally manipulated by her.

483
00:27:02,162 --> 00:27:03,705
- Exactly.
- Seriously?

484
00:27:03,788 --> 00:27:06,708
Do you really think she's capable of
something like that? I mean, look at her.

485
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:09,544
In order to get
another helping of donkkaseu,

486
00:27:09,628 --> 00:27:12,422
she's trying to disguise herself
by going like this with her hair.

487
00:27:12,505 --> 00:27:15,759
Does that look like an evil genius to you?
Come on.

488
00:27:20,639 --> 00:27:24,100
Okay, our first patient is Park
Gwang-cheol, 67 years old.

489
00:27:24,184 --> 00:27:27,020
He's a VIP who has generously
supported the hospital over the years.

490
00:27:27,103 --> 00:27:31,191
We must make every effort to ensure
he is comfortable during his stay here.

491
00:27:31,274 --> 00:27:34,027
And Dr. Do Yun-sik
will be the primary surgeon.

492
00:27:34,110 --> 00:27:36,696
Oh, so that guy's a VIP?

493
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:39,783
The diagnosis is cancer in
the head of the pancreas,

494
00:27:39,866 --> 00:27:41,701
measuring about 4 cm.

495
00:27:42,243 --> 00:27:44,996
So we decided that the Whipple Procedure
is the best option.

496
00:27:45,080 --> 00:27:46,581
- I'll do my best--
- I object.

497
00:27:50,043 --> 00:27:53,338
There's a possibility the cancer
has invaded the SMA or SMV.

498
00:27:53,421 --> 00:27:55,173
Even if it has, it's the same plan.

499
00:27:55,674 --> 00:27:57,676
The VIP has refused chemotherapy.

500
00:27:58,802 --> 00:28:00,011
Ah, first of all,

501
00:28:00,095 --> 00:28:02,514
I'll try to preserve the SMA
as much as possible during the surgery.

502
00:28:02,597 --> 00:28:03,640
If you leave the blood vessels,

503
00:28:03,723 --> 00:28:05,642
it'll be an R2 resection.
Why even operate then?

504
00:28:05,725 --> 00:28:08,061
After surgery, he'll get the chemotherapy.

505
00:28:08,144 --> 00:28:11,231
You should resect it along
with the blood vessel, R0.

506
00:28:11,314 --> 00:28:13,441
- Unbelievable.
- R0?

507
00:28:14,067 --> 00:28:15,819
She is driving me crazy.

508
00:28:17,362 --> 00:28:21,282
R0? Do you think we don't do that
because we don't want to?

509
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:22,659
You trying to sabotage us?

510
00:28:22,742 --> 00:28:26,413
It's basic surgical knowledge
you don't mess with the SMA.

511
00:28:26,496 --> 00:28:27,497
Or don't you know that?

512
00:28:28,081 --> 00:28:29,374
Geez.

513
00:28:30,208 --> 00:28:34,087
I'd be okay with messing with it,
but I guess you wouldn't be.

514
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:38,675
Are you saying you can do it, Dr. Gye?

515
00:28:39,342 --> 00:28:41,720
- Yes.
- So you'd do it yourself?

516
00:28:41,803 --> 00:28:44,264
- Mmm.
- If you fail, this hospital--

517
00:28:44,347 --> 00:28:45,473
Except…

518
00:28:47,183 --> 00:28:48,601
it's not in my nature to fail.

519
00:28:55,817 --> 00:28:58,987
Okay, the next patient is Lee Ju-hui,
a 15-year-old female.

520
00:28:59,070 --> 00:29:00,947
Dr. Do Yun-sik is her attending.

521
00:29:01,030 --> 00:29:03,158
The VIP requested
that his surgery be moved up,

522
00:29:03,241 --> 00:29:07,162
so Lee Ju-hui has agreed
to have her surgery postponed--

523
00:29:07,245 --> 00:29:08,913
Lee Ju-hui's surgery…

524
00:29:10,623 --> 00:29:12,500
will be performed by Dr. Gye.

525
00:29:14,169 --> 00:29:15,503
Director.

526
00:29:15,587 --> 00:29:17,839
This patient is crucial to my case report.

527
00:29:18,465 --> 00:29:20,300
- I wanna keep her.
- And I really don't want her.

528
00:29:20,383 --> 00:29:23,011
You think it's acceptable
to postpone a surgery?

529
00:29:23,094 --> 00:29:24,763
Explain her case.

530
00:29:24,846 --> 00:29:26,055
Ah, right.

531
00:29:26,139 --> 00:29:28,641
She has an 8 cm tumor
in the pancreatic body and tail.

532
00:29:28,725 --> 00:29:30,101
Uh, based on the imaging,

533
00:29:30,185 --> 00:29:32,645
further evaluation for pancreatoblastoma
was recommended,

534
00:29:32,729 --> 00:29:35,023
so we performed
an ultrasound-guided biopsy,

535
00:29:35,106 --> 00:29:36,399
which confirmed the diagnosis.

536
00:29:37,108 --> 00:29:39,360
There was no evidence
of distant metastasis.

537
00:29:52,999 --> 00:29:54,000
She's back.

538
00:29:56,419 --> 00:29:59,130
Don't cause trouble, or you'll get fired.

539
00:29:59,672 --> 00:30:01,257
Keep a low profile.

540
00:30:01,341 --> 00:30:02,967
It's not like they won't let you operate.

541
00:30:03,051 --> 00:30:05,178
You really think
she can keep a low profile?

542
00:30:05,261 --> 00:30:06,429
You know how she is.

543
00:30:07,847 --> 00:30:10,850
- Whoa! I almost dropped it.
- Whoa.

544
00:30:12,644 --> 00:30:16,856
You know, if Dr. Do performs the surgery,
he could kill someone.

545
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:20,735
That's how it's done.

546
00:30:21,361 --> 00:30:22,570
Is he really that bad?

547
00:30:22,654 --> 00:30:24,864
He got where he is through papers,
research and cronyism.

548
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:26,449
Not because he has skills.

549
00:30:26,950 --> 00:30:29,619
The hospital doctor's world is built on…

550
00:30:30,453 --> 00:30:31,496
their rep,

551
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:33,289
prestige,

552
00:30:33,373 --> 00:30:34,415
and authority.

553
00:30:35,041 --> 00:30:37,377
And a lot of other factors
that support that world.

554
00:30:37,460 --> 00:30:40,004
Take those away,
and they wouldn't be doctors.

555
00:30:40,088 --> 00:30:42,549
If they wouldn't be doctors without them,
then they weren't doctors

556
00:30:42,632 --> 00:30:44,884
- in the first place.
- Hey. And when those things…

557
00:30:46,594 --> 00:30:48,596
…collapse,

558
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:50,223
that's our opportunity.

559
00:30:51,015 --> 00:30:53,393
Oh, for Jenga's sake.

560
00:30:56,145 --> 00:30:58,022
Bend over. Here we go.

561
00:30:58,106 --> 00:30:59,983
Loser's punishment.

562
00:31:00,066 --> 00:31:02,777
She must be fueled by blind ambition.

563
00:31:03,444 --> 00:31:05,488
I mean, Lee Ju-hui's a patient too.

564
00:31:06,322 --> 00:31:08,783
Maybe she gets paid more
for surgery on a VIP.

565
00:31:09,534 --> 00:31:10,743
Watch her tomorrow too.

566
00:31:11,286 --> 00:31:12,871
And tell her to go apologize.

567
00:31:14,038 --> 00:31:15,123
I'm off.

568
00:31:15,206 --> 00:31:17,417
- Okay. Have a good night.
- See ya.

569
00:31:29,679 --> 00:31:32,974
Just in case she comes back here tomorrow…

570
00:31:44,152 --> 00:31:47,864
Complications include pancreatic fistula,
peritonitis, infections,

571
00:31:47,947 --> 00:31:51,200
blood clots, lung and heart complications,
bowel obstruction,

572
00:31:51,284 --> 00:31:53,745
and the possibility
of postoperative bleeding.

573
00:31:54,662 --> 00:31:56,372
So, do you have any questions for us?

574
00:31:56,456 --> 00:31:59,667
Oh, uh, could I just ask,
what happened to the other doctor?

575
00:31:59,751 --> 00:32:02,378
I thought he was a big shot around here,
so…

576
00:32:02,462 --> 00:32:05,089
Oh, she's really skilled too.
You can take it from me.

577
00:32:05,173 --> 00:32:06,674
- Ah.
- Seriously?

578
00:32:07,258 --> 00:32:09,218
He said I was an extremely rare case
or whatever

579
00:32:09,302 --> 00:32:12,138
and that he wanted
to do the surgery himself.

580
00:32:12,221 --> 00:32:13,348
What a joke.

581
00:32:14,933 --> 00:32:17,518
How long will she be in surgery?

582
00:32:17,602 --> 00:32:20,355
Uh, we think it will take around
three to four hours to complete.

583
00:32:20,438 --> 00:32:21,856
Oh.

584
00:32:21,940 --> 00:32:23,691
- That's so long.
- Mm-hmm.

585
00:32:25,610 --> 00:32:27,028
I don't want the operation.

586
00:32:28,780 --> 00:32:30,740
- Sorry?
- What are you talking about?

587
00:32:30,823 --> 00:32:32,116
What, are you nuts?

588
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:33,201
Hey.

589
00:32:33,284 --> 00:32:36,120
You can't back out now.
We already cashed in your college fund.

590
00:32:36,204 --> 00:32:38,122
Your focus needs to be
on the surgery right now.

591
00:32:38,206 --> 00:32:42,210
Even if I live, no college
is ever gonna want to accept me.

592
00:32:43,169 --> 00:32:45,254
That's why I always tell you
to study or work.

593
00:32:45,338 --> 00:32:46,464
I looked it up too.

594
00:32:46,547 --> 00:32:49,634
It said that my chances
are really not very good.

595
00:32:50,593 --> 00:32:52,971
For someone like me, it's usually this,
isn't it?

596
00:32:53,054 --> 00:32:54,389
Geez.

597
00:32:54,973 --> 00:32:58,184
That damned Internet.
It totally messes kids up.

598
00:32:58,267 --> 00:33:01,729
Uh, don't pay attention to her. We're fine
with that doctor doing the surgery. Okay?

599
00:33:01,813 --> 00:33:03,606
Miss, you need to get the surgery--

600
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:04,941
Ju-hui.

601
00:33:05,692 --> 00:33:08,820
- How dare you say you won't even try?
- Stop it, both of you. Okay?

602
00:33:08,903 --> 00:33:10,488
Give me the consent form.
We'll just sign it now

603
00:33:10,571 --> 00:33:12,907
and go outside to fight among ourselves.

604
00:33:12,991 --> 00:33:14,742
No, miss, please give that back.

605
00:33:14,826 --> 00:33:15,702
- Ju-hui!
- I'm sick of this.

606
00:33:15,785 --> 00:33:17,912
- Hey!
- Just let me talk!

607
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:22,125
I'm sick of all this, that's why.
I'm tired, Mom.

608
00:33:22,208 --> 00:33:23,584
I'm only 15 years old.

609
00:33:24,419 --> 00:33:25,920
Do you know what
the other kids are saying?

610
00:33:26,713 --> 00:33:28,381
They call me a junkie

611
00:33:28,464 --> 00:33:31,009
because I give myself
injections in the bathoom every day.

612
00:33:33,594 --> 00:33:36,222
If you didn't get your insulin shots,
you'd die. They don't know anything.

613
00:33:36,305 --> 00:33:38,558
But now I have a deadly illness
on top of that.

614
00:33:39,142 --> 00:33:40,727
And, Mom, you've got your health problems.

615
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:44,313
It's gotta be really hard
to take care of me as well.

616
00:33:46,941 --> 00:33:48,151
I'm your mom. It's not hard.

617
00:33:48,234 --> 00:33:49,527
Then what about you, Auntie?

618
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:53,114
You've probably
got it the worst of all of us.

619
00:33:53,906 --> 00:33:56,743
You've got a dying niece
and a disabled sister to care for.

620
00:33:56,826 --> 00:33:59,162
You have to work twice as hard
as everyone else because of us,

621
00:33:59,245 --> 00:34:00,830
then come home and do work at the house.

622
00:34:01,873 --> 00:34:03,041
You deserve better than that.

623
00:34:03,541 --> 00:34:04,792
I can handle it.

624
00:34:05,668 --> 00:34:07,628
I can't handle you giving up though.
Give me that.

625
00:34:07,712 --> 00:34:09,088
Stop it!

626
00:34:09,172 --> 00:34:10,298
Just leave me alone.

627
00:34:11,090 --> 00:34:13,968
Just… just go, all of you.

628
00:34:14,052 --> 00:34:15,762
Just let me die!

629
00:34:15,845 --> 00:34:17,638
We all die sometime, don't we?

630
00:34:21,517 --> 00:34:22,518
So, there's no rush.

631
00:34:22,602 --> 00:34:25,480
You could die today or next week.
It makes no difference in the long run.

632
00:34:25,563 --> 00:34:28,274
- Dr. Gye, maybe don't mention--
- It's all the same.

633
00:34:29,609 --> 00:34:32,695
But if I don't operate,
you'll be dead within a month.

634
00:34:32,779 --> 00:34:34,697
And if you get the surgery,
you'll still die.

635
00:34:34,781 --> 00:34:35,990
But it won't be for…

636
00:34:36,616 --> 00:34:37,617
a hundred years or so.

637
00:34:37,700 --> 00:34:39,368
She's 15, that's about right, isn't it?

638
00:34:40,119 --> 00:34:41,120
Uh, well…

639
00:34:41,204 --> 00:34:44,582
And only if I do your surgery.

640
00:34:45,583 --> 00:34:46,793
Because I never fail.

641
00:34:47,627 --> 00:34:50,296
I'll save you. No matter what it takes.

642
00:34:57,345 --> 00:34:58,346
Your choice.

643
00:34:59,013 --> 00:35:02,016
Do you wanna die in a month,
or live for a hundred years?

644
00:35:03,434 --> 00:35:06,479
"Do you wanna die in a month,
or live for a hundred years?"

645
00:35:07,688 --> 00:35:10,858
Wow. That whole time
I kept explaining things to them.

646
00:35:10,942 --> 00:35:14,070
And your line worked like magic.

647
00:35:14,153 --> 00:35:15,988
If you fail, though,
we'll be in serious trouble.

648
00:35:16,572 --> 00:35:18,741
Of course we will. Someone could die.

649
00:35:18,825 --> 00:35:20,118
But you…

650
00:35:20,201 --> 00:35:23,246
I mean, come on. You've been studying
her chart nonstop since…

651
00:35:23,913 --> 00:35:25,039
Wait, what's this?

652
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:27,291
You've been reading Chairman Park's chart
this whole time?

653
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:28,459
Dr. Gye.

654
00:35:32,421 --> 00:35:34,882
When you do Lee Ju-hui's surgery,
please do your best.

655
00:35:34,966 --> 00:35:36,926
I mean, I could do it, but…

656
00:35:37,009 --> 00:35:39,303
…as you know, Director Bu
has me doing Chairman Park's surgery.

657
00:35:39,387 --> 00:35:41,180
We got the consent form signed today.

658
00:35:41,264 --> 00:35:43,099
You might wanna consider
switching surgeries with me.

659
00:35:43,182 --> 00:35:44,392
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

660
00:35:50,356 --> 00:35:52,942
And why is it that you keep saying that?

661
00:35:53,442 --> 00:35:54,735
You don't have the skills to do it.

662
00:35:54,819 --> 00:35:56,529
- Okay, that's it!
- Please don't.

663
00:35:57,238 --> 00:35:59,866
If only you were as competent
as you are stubborn.

664
00:35:59,949 --> 00:36:02,660
We can hear you.
We heard that loud and clear!

665
00:36:02,743 --> 00:36:04,662
Doctor, people are watching.
Please calm down, Dr. Ma.

666
00:36:04,745 --> 00:36:06,164
Oh, so that's how it us, huh?

667
00:36:09,125 --> 00:36:12,170
Oh, boy!

668
00:36:13,421 --> 00:36:14,797
Hey, wait.

669
00:36:14,881 --> 00:36:16,757
Su-jeong, come eat!

670
00:36:19,385 --> 00:36:22,054
- She must be preparing for surgery.
- Mm-hmm.

671
00:36:22,138 --> 00:36:24,599
Surgery is the only thing
she likes more than eating.

672
00:36:24,682 --> 00:36:28,060
Only one each! I cooked one per person.

673
00:36:32,356 --> 00:36:33,608
Hey, aren't you two ever going home?

674
00:36:33,691 --> 00:36:35,610
You're both eating three meals a day here.

675
00:36:35,693 --> 00:36:37,820
Oh! Are we celebrating?

676
00:36:37,904 --> 00:36:39,447
- Because you made galbijjim.
- Uh, yeah.

677
00:36:40,781 --> 00:36:43,117
Kimchi. Mmm.

678
00:36:43,201 --> 00:36:46,245
DOCTOR DO YUN-SIK

679
00:36:58,216 --> 00:37:00,051
You don't have the skills to do it.

680
00:37:00,968 --> 00:37:02,929
Lee Ju-hui's surgery

681
00:37:03,012 --> 00:37:04,889
will be performed by Dr. Gye.

682
00:37:43,886 --> 00:37:44,887
Found it.

683
00:37:48,808 --> 00:37:50,851
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

684
00:37:56,565 --> 00:37:59,610
Oh, Lee Ju-hui's pancreatic cancer surgery
is today as well, isn't it?

685
00:37:59,694 --> 00:38:01,279
Where is it, OR 5?

686
00:38:01,362 --> 00:38:02,863
It's not too late to switch.

687
00:38:18,379 --> 00:38:19,797
Let's do a time-out.

688
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:22,049
Please stop what you're doing
and pay attention.

689
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:24,552
What is the patient's name
and registration number?

690
00:38:24,635 --> 00:38:28,097
11384675, Park Gwang-cheol.

691
00:38:29,348 --> 00:38:31,058
OPERATION TIME, TIME, ANESTHESIA TIME

692
00:38:34,854 --> 00:38:35,855
Scalpel.

693
00:38:41,527 --> 00:38:44,113
No issues with anesthesia,
and vitals are stable.

694
00:38:44,613 --> 00:38:47,950
Then we'll begin with
the time-out. Lee Ju-hui's sub--

695
00:39:20,024 --> 00:39:21,025
Wipe.

696
00:39:25,863 --> 00:39:26,864
Harmonic.

697
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:30,201
Wipe.

698
00:39:39,085 --> 00:39:40,294
Vessel loop.

699
00:39:47,426 --> 00:39:48,844
Long Kelly.

700
00:39:57,436 --> 00:39:59,063
I can see the SMA.

701
00:39:59,897 --> 00:40:02,149
Does that surprise you?

702
00:40:02,233 --> 00:40:04,568
It's like you've never seen it before.

703
00:40:17,581 --> 00:40:18,666
This…

704
00:40:19,750 --> 00:40:21,043
It shouldn't be like this.

705
00:40:21,585 --> 00:40:22,628
What's wrong, Doctor?

706
00:40:25,589 --> 00:40:28,300
It's spread too much.

707
00:40:29,427 --> 00:40:31,512
It's much worse than I expected.

708
00:40:32,430 --> 00:40:33,431
The tumor…

709
00:40:34,723 --> 00:40:37,184
- It's completely…
- It's encasing the vessel.

710
00:40:37,268 --> 00:40:40,271
The SMA invasion is pervasive.

711
00:40:42,148 --> 00:40:43,274
Yun-sik…

712
00:40:44,900 --> 00:40:46,152
What are you going to do?

713
00:41:02,084 --> 00:41:03,961
Even if we do a partial resection,

714
00:41:04,044 --> 00:41:05,921
the prognosis won't change.

715
00:41:06,005 --> 00:41:07,047
We'll have to…

716
00:41:08,757 --> 00:41:10,009
close him back up.

717
00:41:12,553 --> 00:41:13,554
Listen to me.

718
00:41:13,637 --> 00:41:16,474
This isn't just any patient.
The fate of the hospital depends on…

719
00:41:16,557 --> 00:41:17,766
The mic.

720
00:41:19,351 --> 00:41:20,352
Dr. Do.

721
00:41:21,353 --> 00:41:23,522
Is your plan really
just to give up trying?

722
00:41:23,606 --> 00:41:25,024
Excuse me?

723
00:41:25,608 --> 00:41:27,234
What if I tell you that's not an option?

724
00:41:27,318 --> 00:41:29,695
But Director, what else can I do?

725
00:41:29,778 --> 00:41:32,740
Any further resection could do the patient
more harm than good.

726
00:41:33,449 --> 00:41:36,368
You're going to tell him you cut into him
just to close him back up again?

727
00:41:36,452 --> 00:41:38,162
But…

728
00:41:38,746 --> 00:41:40,831
Wouldn't it be better if you could say

729
00:41:40,915 --> 00:41:43,667
you did everything you possibly could
until the very end?

730
00:41:57,640 --> 00:42:00,309
Then if we could contact
the patient's family…

731
00:42:01,143 --> 00:42:02,353
There is no one.

732
00:42:02,436 --> 00:42:04,021
There's no one here. Why would they be?

733
00:42:04,104 --> 00:42:05,481
Damn it…

734
00:42:08,609 --> 00:42:10,319
They're all just waiting for him to die.

735
00:42:11,487 --> 00:42:13,572
His family keeps calling,
one right after the other,

736
00:42:13,656 --> 00:42:15,449
to check on his chances of survival.

737
00:42:27,086 --> 00:42:28,546
Bu Seung-gwon calling.

738
00:42:33,217 --> 00:42:34,718
You know we're not religious.

739
00:42:35,219 --> 00:42:36,762
I'm trying everything I can.

740
00:42:37,304 --> 00:42:38,973
Should we start
believing in something now?

741
00:42:39,056 --> 00:42:40,724
I will if Ju-hui gets better.

742
00:42:41,559 --> 00:42:42,977
If she doesn't, I won't.

743
00:42:45,271 --> 00:42:46,480
It'll be their loss.

744
00:42:49,817 --> 00:42:51,860
Why don't you get something to eat?

745
00:42:51,944 --> 00:42:52,945
No, I'm okay.

746
00:42:53,028 --> 00:42:55,072
Ju-hui didn't eat before her surgery,

747
00:42:56,115 --> 00:42:57,449
and neither should I.

748
00:43:04,498 --> 00:43:06,333
There's a chocolate bar in there.
Help yourself.

749
00:43:13,674 --> 00:43:14,675
Unnie.

750
00:43:16,468 --> 00:43:17,595
Look what I found.

751
00:43:17,678 --> 00:43:19,346
TO MY FAMILY

752
00:43:25,811 --> 00:43:27,354
Transecting the pancreas.

753
00:43:27,438 --> 00:43:29,148
Stapler, 60, black.

754
00:43:33,694 --> 00:43:34,695
Thank goodness.

755
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:36,655
The adhesion isn't severe.

756
00:43:37,656 --> 00:43:39,325
It is still pretty big though.

757
00:43:46,749 --> 00:43:48,834
I'll get it, Dr. Gye.
Focus on the surgery.

758
00:43:49,543 --> 00:43:51,712
- Hello. This is OR 5.
- Right angle.

759
00:43:51,795 --> 00:43:54,548
Uh, this is Park Tae-gyeong, the intern.
Go ahead.

760
00:43:57,676 --> 00:43:58,677
Not bad.

761
00:43:59,762 --> 00:44:03,515
Tell Dr. Gye…
she's needed in OR 1 right away.

762
00:44:04,308 --> 00:44:05,309
Sorry?

763
00:44:06,268 --> 00:44:09,897
Uh, Dr. Gye is in the middle of surgery
at the moment.

764
00:44:09,980 --> 00:44:11,815
Tell her it's an emergency.

765
00:44:17,613 --> 00:44:19,740
Uh, I'm sorry, Director. I can't do that.

766
00:44:19,823 --> 00:44:21,283
We need more time here.

767
00:44:21,367 --> 00:44:23,702
Dr. Gye has to stay
and finish this surgery.

768
00:44:25,371 --> 00:44:27,206
This is Gye Su-jeong. I'll be right there.

769
00:44:29,625 --> 00:44:30,959
Dr. Gye?

770
00:44:31,043 --> 00:44:33,253
Are you giving up on Ju-hui's surgery?

771
00:44:33,337 --> 00:44:35,255
- Out of the way.
- Why would you do that?

772
00:44:35,339 --> 00:44:36,548
Because she's not a VIP?

773
00:44:36,632 --> 00:44:38,634
Because she's from a poor family
with a disabled mother?

774
00:44:38,717 --> 00:44:39,802
Priority.

775
00:44:39,885 --> 00:44:42,805
So, by priority,
do you mean getting ahead?

776
00:44:42,888 --> 00:44:45,224
Is that the kind of doctor you are?

777
00:44:45,307 --> 00:44:46,475
I said get out of the way.

778
00:44:46,558 --> 00:44:48,727
Whenever the other doctors
would bad-mouth you

779
00:44:48,811 --> 00:44:50,854
for chasing money and success,

780
00:44:50,938 --> 00:44:52,898
I never believed it. But now…

781
00:44:52,981 --> 00:44:54,566
How could you do this?

782
00:44:55,818 --> 00:44:57,069
You're a doctor!

783
00:44:57,152 --> 00:44:59,446
You should look after your patient
until the end!

784
00:44:59,530 --> 00:45:01,073
You promised her a hundred years!

785
00:45:01,865 --> 00:45:03,742
You said you'd save her
no matter what it takes.

786
00:45:13,627 --> 00:45:15,003
That's more like it.

787
00:45:33,647 --> 00:45:34,898
<i>You're a doctor!</i>

788
00:45:34,982 --> 00:45:37,067
<i>You should look after your patient</i>
<i>until the end!</i>

789
00:45:37,151 --> 00:45:38,694
<i>You promised her a hundred years!</i>

790
00:45:39,278 --> 00:45:41,321
<i>You said you'd save her</i>
<i>no matter what it takes.</i>

791
00:45:50,706 --> 00:45:53,459
- Uh, what? How…
- I called Doctor Gye in.

792
00:45:53,542 --> 00:45:55,586
- Director!
- I'm taking over.

793
00:45:57,212 --> 00:45:59,256
Director, you can't do this!

794
00:45:59,339 --> 00:46:01,467
Wait a sec. I don't…

795
00:46:01,550 --> 00:46:04,803
- What about the surgery in OR 5 then?
- Go see if you're worried.

796
00:46:04,887 --> 00:46:06,513
Oh, you're such a b--

797
00:46:07,890 --> 00:46:10,851
Are you out of your mind?
Did you just abandon your patient?

798
00:46:10,934 --> 00:46:12,770
Dr. Bae Heung-gon is already there.

799
00:46:13,896 --> 00:46:16,106
Hey, move, move it! And let me through.

800
00:46:17,524 --> 00:46:18,942
Move! Out of my way!

801
00:46:19,735 --> 00:46:20,694
Dr. Gye.

802
00:46:21,236 --> 00:46:22,863
He's all yours, I'm counting on you.

803
00:46:39,588 --> 00:46:43,175
- Just as I thought. Move aside, please.
- What are you going to do?

804
00:46:55,312 --> 00:46:59,775
RESECTION PHASE
(RESECTION AND VASCULAR DISSECTION)

805
00:47:05,322 --> 00:47:07,324
I'm going to do a saphenous harvest.

806
00:47:07,407 --> 00:47:09,368
- What?
- Open the drape and disinfect the leg.

807
00:47:09,451 --> 00:47:10,994
Scissors, please.

808
00:47:11,078 --> 00:47:12,246
W-why the leg?

809
00:47:12,746 --> 00:47:14,122
What do you think you're doing?

810
00:47:14,206 --> 00:47:16,166
Why are you changing procedure
all of a sudden? Hey, the next surgery--

811
00:47:16,250 --> 00:47:18,502
Get Dr. Jo Won-jin from OR 5, please.

812
00:47:18,585 --> 00:47:20,587
What? Hey!

813
00:47:20,671 --> 00:47:24,633
I'm on it. Dr. Kim, please go to OR 5.

814
00:47:24,716 --> 00:47:26,844
That shouldn't be necessary.

815
00:47:32,307 --> 00:47:34,059
Hold mean BP at 70.

816
00:47:34,142 --> 00:47:35,769
- Yes, Doctor.
- Dr. Jo, seriously? You too?

817
00:47:35,853 --> 00:47:37,437
How can you abandon your patient?

818
00:47:37,521 --> 00:47:40,315
If only you were this concerned
about professional ethics all the time.

819
00:47:44,695 --> 00:47:46,864
- What's the EBL?
- 100 cc.

820
00:47:48,532 --> 00:47:50,367
Prepare for vascular anastomosis.

821
00:47:50,450 --> 00:47:52,202
Get the 7-0 Prolene and the loupes ready.

822
00:47:52,286 --> 00:47:54,037
Don't tell me you're going to…

823
00:47:55,330 --> 00:47:56,331
cut the vessel.

824
00:47:56,415 --> 00:47:59,751
I guess writing all those papers
actually gave you a decent eye.

825
00:47:59,835 --> 00:48:00,836
You there.

826
00:48:01,336 --> 00:48:02,713
I'd like you to assist me.

827
00:48:02,796 --> 00:48:04,464
You wanna cut the vessel?

828
00:48:04,548 --> 00:48:06,550
How do I assist
when I don't know what you're doing?

829
00:48:08,510 --> 00:48:13,056
We're doing an en bloc resection
of the pancreatic head, including the SMA.

830
00:48:13,140 --> 00:48:14,308
What?

831
00:48:14,391 --> 00:48:16,727
Huh? Uh, wait…

832
00:48:27,446 --> 00:48:28,697
So you're saying…

833
00:48:29,740 --> 00:48:32,659
that she did all of this in an hour?

834
00:48:33,744 --> 00:48:36,079
Yes, Doctor.

835
00:48:36,163 --> 00:48:37,789
Did the surgery go well?

836
00:48:38,749 --> 00:48:39,958
In just an hour?

837
00:48:40,584 --> 00:48:41,752
There isn't even any blood.

838
00:48:41,835 --> 00:48:43,462
What kind of doctor talks that?

839
00:48:44,129 --> 00:48:45,255
Sorry?

840
00:48:45,797 --> 00:48:46,924
Hemostasis.

841
00:48:47,007 --> 00:48:51,136
Uh, right. Right. Uh, the hemostasis
was complete according to Dr. Jo Won-jin.

842
00:48:52,888 --> 00:48:53,889
So this…

843
00:48:55,515 --> 00:48:57,476
This is Gye Su-jeong's work?

844
00:48:58,477 --> 00:49:00,854
After harvesting the saphenous vein
from the thigh,

845
00:49:00,938 --> 00:49:04,358
we'll proceed with the en bloc resection
of the pancreatic cancer,

846
00:49:04,441 --> 00:49:06,485
including the SMA and SMV.

847
00:49:06,568 --> 00:49:09,279
We will reconstruct the SMA
with the saphenous vein,

848
00:49:09,363 --> 00:49:11,490
and use an 8 mm synthetic graft
for the SMV.

849
00:49:11,573 --> 00:49:12,991
W-wait!

850
00:49:13,075 --> 00:49:14,368
What did you just say?

851
00:49:14,451 --> 00:49:17,204
Doctor, is she-- Is she really gonna…

852
00:49:17,287 --> 00:49:19,665
Have you lost your mind?
Are you practicing on a patient?

853
00:49:19,748 --> 00:49:21,959
- Are you really gonna do this?
- Yes, I am.

854
00:49:22,042 --> 00:49:23,794
There's no telling what might happen!
It's too risky!

855
00:49:23,877 --> 00:49:27,047
If you fail, he'll die.
He'll die from bowel necrosis!

856
00:49:27,130 --> 00:49:28,340
Dr. Do Yun-sik.

857
00:49:30,842 --> 00:49:32,427
Do it Dr. Gye Su-jeong's way.

858
00:49:33,470 --> 00:49:38,475
And, by the way, Doctor Gye Su-jeong
was not in this operating room today.

859
00:49:42,980 --> 00:49:44,773
Self-retaining retractor
and loupes, please.

860
00:50:49,796 --> 00:50:51,131
Harmonic.

861
00:51:02,642 --> 00:51:05,479
Estimated blood loss is 320 ccs.

862
00:51:05,562 --> 00:51:07,314
The bowel anastomosis is complete.

863
00:51:07,856 --> 00:51:10,817
Please monitor the drain output closely
for any signs of bleeding.

864
00:51:10,901 --> 00:51:13,028
You can do that yourself, Dr. Gye…

865
00:51:13,820 --> 00:51:16,865
Oh, don't tell me you're clocking out now…

866
00:51:16,948 --> 00:51:20,577
You should at least do this much.
If you want to call yourself a doctor.

867
00:51:46,770 --> 00:51:48,188
Director.

868
00:51:48,271 --> 00:51:51,733
Since she did two surgeries today,
we'll have to charge double.

869
00:51:52,359 --> 00:51:54,986
And neither the patient's family,
nor the public,

870
00:51:55,070 --> 00:51:56,988
will hear about this from us.

871
00:51:58,406 --> 00:52:01,993
- I understand.
- In return, we'd like payment in cash.

872
00:52:02,911 --> 00:52:03,912
I'll be back soon.

873
00:52:42,367 --> 00:52:43,535
Sir, I'm sorry.

874
00:52:44,786 --> 00:52:45,912
Yun-sik.

875
00:52:46,997 --> 00:52:49,499
Closing him back up
was your first instinct.

876
00:52:51,126 --> 00:52:53,170
You didn't think about
what else you could have done.

877
00:52:54,171 --> 00:52:56,089
Your first instinct was to give up.

878
00:52:56,173 --> 00:52:57,841
- But--
- And by that point,

879
00:52:59,176 --> 00:53:00,802
you were basically gone.

880
00:53:03,722 --> 00:53:05,015
I was there though.

881
00:53:08,685 --> 00:53:09,936
I offered to assist

882
00:53:10,562 --> 00:53:12,314
and I stayed until the end of surgery.

883
00:53:14,191 --> 00:53:15,400
Just so I could do something.

884
00:53:16,359 --> 00:53:18,570
Can you imagine how humiliated I felt?

885
00:53:20,113 --> 00:53:21,656
Facing that insurmountable wall,

886
00:53:21,740 --> 00:53:25,577
knowing that I don't have the skills to…
to get over the top.

887
00:53:27,996 --> 00:53:28,997
I…

888
00:53:33,126 --> 00:53:34,336
But I still…

889
00:53:35,170 --> 00:53:37,589
I still stayed in the OR the whole time.

890
00:53:37,672 --> 00:53:38,798
I persevered.

891
00:53:40,800 --> 00:53:42,344
And I'll continue to persevere.

892
00:53:42,928 --> 00:53:43,970
And…

893
00:53:47,057 --> 00:53:50,477
I know I'm gonna make a name for myself
here one day. I want to.

894
00:53:51,478 --> 00:53:53,396
And fulfill every one of my dreams.

895
00:53:54,773 --> 00:53:55,774
Director.

896
00:53:56,733 --> 00:53:57,817
You know…

897
00:54:01,863 --> 00:54:02,906
…what my dream is.

898
00:54:09,663 --> 00:54:10,705
I do.

899
00:54:12,374 --> 00:54:13,375
I understand.

900
00:54:24,844 --> 00:54:29,015
That guy can be really sappy.

901
00:54:29,557 --> 00:54:31,268
He's not a very good surgeon either.

902
00:54:31,351 --> 00:54:32,894
But it was pretty cool of him to say.

903
00:54:33,812 --> 00:54:34,813
Mm-hmm.

904
00:54:36,439 --> 00:54:38,191
Uh, what are you two doing there?

905
00:54:38,984 --> 00:54:40,860
Uh, h-have you seen Dr. Gye?

906
00:54:40,944 --> 00:54:44,406
Ugh. I'm so sick of hearing that name.

907
00:54:44,489 --> 00:54:45,573
Gye Su-jeong.

908
00:54:46,074 --> 00:54:48,326
You're going a little overboard
with the surveillance thing.

909
00:54:48,410 --> 00:54:51,413
Yeah, what would she be doing here,
in the men's locker room?

910
00:54:51,496 --> 00:54:52,706
Oh, right.

911
00:54:53,290 --> 00:54:55,583
- What?
- Well, it's just that earlier…

912
00:54:57,043 --> 00:54:58,420
It's nothing.

913
00:54:58,503 --> 00:54:59,587
Huh.

914
00:55:01,089 --> 00:55:02,924
Uh, she really did two surgeries
in an hour?

915
00:55:03,008 --> 00:55:04,467
Yeah.

916
00:55:04,551 --> 00:55:05,760
And what I think?

917
00:55:05,844 --> 00:55:09,306
She planned it. She knew that she was
gonna have to do both surgeries.

918
00:55:09,389 --> 00:55:11,599
- It's the only explanation.
- For real?

919
00:55:11,683 --> 00:55:12,809
Oh, shit.

920
00:55:12,892 --> 00:55:15,145
I had no idea.

921
00:55:15,729 --> 00:55:17,605
Gosh. I'll be on my way then.

922
00:55:21,192 --> 00:55:22,444
What's with that guy?

923
00:56:22,379 --> 00:56:24,798
TO MY FAMILY
MY AUNT, ME, MY MOM

924
00:56:24,881 --> 00:56:26,174
<i>To my family.</i>

925
00:56:27,717 --> 00:56:29,552
<i>Mom, Auntie</i>…

926
00:56:29,636 --> 00:56:33,098
<i>Forget a hundred years.</i>
<i>I might end up dying today.</i>

927
00:56:34,182 --> 00:56:38,895
<i>Mom, Auntie, you two only love me</i>
<i>because I'm your daughter and niece.</i>

928
00:56:39,646 --> 00:56:42,941
<i>If I weren't, you wouldn't have</i>
<i>liked me that much.</i>

929
00:56:43,983 --> 00:56:46,611
<i>But I think I would have liked you both,</i>

930
00:56:47,320 --> 00:56:51,074
<i>even if you weren't my mom or my aunt.</i>

931
00:56:53,410 --> 00:56:57,288
<i>You two are really amazing</i>
<i>and wonderful people.</i>

932
00:56:58,623 --> 00:57:00,417
<i>That's what I really wanted to say,</i>

933
00:57:01,376 --> 00:57:04,087
<i>instead of something like, "I love you."</i>

934
00:57:05,672 --> 00:57:08,258
- Yeah, that's right. He's out of surgery.
- It was you, wasn't it?

935
00:57:08,341 --> 00:57:10,969
No, it wasn't me.
I was on your side, if you recall.

936
00:57:11,052 --> 00:57:12,220
That's not true at all.

937
00:57:12,303 --> 00:57:14,722
What are you talking about?
I said we should do it all together.

938
00:57:14,806 --> 00:57:16,307
- Oh, come on.
- You don't remember?

939
00:57:16,391 --> 00:57:18,184
You've been blocking me
every step of the way.

940
00:57:18,268 --> 00:57:19,519
Don't you think I know that?

941
00:57:20,353 --> 00:57:23,440
I can't imagine why you would
feel that way. It makes no sense.

942
00:57:26,443 --> 00:57:29,821
<i>Next time we meet, let's be friends.</i>

943
00:57:30,780 --> 00:57:33,116
<i>Instead of always</i>
<i>looking after each other,</i>

944
00:57:33,741 --> 00:57:36,828
<i>let's just have fun together.</i>

945
00:57:38,663 --> 00:57:40,331
<i>Let's make sure we meet again.</i>

946
00:57:55,597 --> 00:57:57,557
- I brought beer.
- Nice!

947
00:57:57,640 --> 00:57:59,851
- Does she know we're having bulgogi?
- Yeah.

948
00:58:00,685 --> 00:58:02,395
Oh, she must be there by now.

949
00:58:02,479 --> 00:58:03,521
My goodness.

950
00:58:03,605 --> 00:58:05,607
The two of you certainly are very excited.

951
00:58:05,690 --> 00:58:08,693
<i>Ooh! You bet, you bet</i>
<i>You bet, you bet!</i>

952
00:58:08,776 --> 00:58:12,363
<i>I'm so excited</i>
<i>Got cash coming down like rain</i>

953
00:58:12,447 --> 00:58:14,073
<i>Filling up my wallet</i>

954
00:58:14,157 --> 00:58:16,618
<i>Making me happy</i>

955
00:58:16,701 --> 00:58:19,996
LUCKY BATHHOUSE

956
00:58:36,054 --> 00:58:38,848
BANANA MILK

957
00:58:40,058 --> 00:58:43,144
You know,
Chairman Park gave this to the hospital

958
00:58:43,228 --> 00:58:46,231
so we could organize a dinner
for the surgical team.

959
00:58:46,314 --> 00:58:49,817
Then all the more reason
for me to take it off your hands.

960
00:59:26,396 --> 00:59:28,189
CHAIRMAN PARK IN RECOVERY
SEARCH AND SEIZURE OF SUN & STEEL

961
00:59:28,273 --> 00:59:32,360
That's right. You need to be alive
to face punishment and pay the price.

962
00:59:33,194 --> 00:59:36,114
Chairman, let's see
how many more years you've got.

963
00:59:50,211 --> 00:59:53,089
Everyone keep looking.
I need that surgical technique in detail.

964
00:59:53,172 --> 00:59:54,257
Okay.

965
00:59:54,340 --> 00:59:56,092
Doctor Gye had to have known beforehand

966
00:59:56,175 --> 00:59:58,261
that she'd need to use
that technique, right?

967
00:59:58,344 --> 00:59:59,679
That's not important right now.

968
01:00:00,263 --> 01:00:02,307
What matters more is what this all means.

969
01:00:02,390 --> 01:00:04,267
So, what does it mean?

970
01:00:08,605 --> 01:00:09,981
That she really is a snake,

971
01:00:10,773 --> 01:00:14,360
who pushes ahead with surgery
that puts her patient's life on the line,

972
01:00:14,444 --> 01:00:15,820
for her own gain.

973
01:00:23,036 --> 01:00:25,330
Doctor Gye, why are you out here
instead of at your desk?

974
01:00:26,456 --> 01:00:28,875
The GS lackeys got rid of my desk.

975
01:00:29,459 --> 01:00:32,170
Uh, the thing is…

976
01:00:32,253 --> 01:00:33,880
It's okay. I'm fine out here.

977
01:00:35,798 --> 01:00:38,468
Well, Ms. Jang has received
what was due for in this case.

978
01:00:38,551 --> 01:00:39,677
It was asking a lot,

979
01:00:40,470 --> 01:00:41,971
and I want you to know I appreciate it.

980
01:00:43,556 --> 01:00:45,058
It wasn't asking that much.

981
01:00:47,018 --> 01:00:48,227
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

982
01:00:51,856 --> 01:00:52,857
<i>Oh, I found it.</i>

983
01:00:54,817 --> 01:00:57,987
Ah, this is the surgical technique
Dr. Gye used.

984
01:00:58,071 --> 01:01:00,365
There's an article about it
from seven years ago.

985
01:01:00,448 --> 01:01:01,449
Hmm.

986
01:01:02,241 --> 01:01:05,995
"Gastrointestinal surgeons
at Cuba's Cubanacan University Hospital

987
01:01:06,079 --> 01:01:08,206
successfully performed
an en bloc resection

988
01:01:08,289 --> 01:01:10,208
with an SMA reconstruction,

989
01:01:11,334 --> 01:01:14,045
providing an unexpected cure
for a patient

990
01:01:14,128 --> 01:01:17,256
who had previously been
considered inoperable.

991
01:01:18,675 --> 01:01:21,344
However, the patient died

992
01:01:21,969 --> 01:01:23,763
two months after the surgery."

993
01:01:31,562 --> 01:01:33,773
You can't avoid failure forever.

994
01:01:41,614 --> 01:01:43,825
It seems like
you've already failed, director.

995
01:01:51,124 --> 01:01:55,128
"The patient's cause of death
is currently unknown."

996
01:02:31,664 --> 01:02:34,333
<i>"The name of the surgeon</i>
<i>was never revealed,</i>

997
01:02:36,043 --> 01:02:38,546
<i>but the alias written on the chart was…</i>

998
01:02:40,047 --> 01:02:41,883
<i>Dr. X."</i>

999
01:02:41,966 --> 01:02:43,217
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

1000
01:03:22,715 --> 01:03:25,635
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

1001
01:03:25,718 --> 01:03:28,679
<i>So you're saying</i>
<i>Dr. Gye Su-jeong is Dr. X?</i>

1002
01:03:28,763 --> 01:03:30,264
What are you doing?

1003
01:03:30,348 --> 01:03:32,350
Right now we're losing blood faster
than we're losing time.

1004
01:03:32,433 --> 01:03:35,144
Don't do it every day! Don't you dare!

1005
01:03:35,228 --> 01:03:37,396
<i>The hospital's been in a tizzy</i>
<i>over the last few days</i>

1006
01:03:37,480 --> 01:03:38,898
<i>- and it's all because of her.</i>
<i>- Transfer her now.</i>

1007
01:03:38,981 --> 01:03:41,442
<i>No. We have to treat her here,</i>
<i>no matter what.</i>

1008
01:03:41,526 --> 01:03:43,486
<i>There's a doctor who can</i>
<i>handle the operation.</i>

1009
01:03:43,569 --> 01:03:46,280
<i>I have temporarily assigned</i>
<i>another doctor here.</i>

1010
01:03:46,364 --> 01:03:48,282
<i>- And who is that?</i>
- The surgery has begun.

1011
01:03:48,366 --> 01:03:49,408
<i>Fire her immediately.</i>

1012
01:03:49,492 --> 01:03:51,911
<i>We need to make sure</i>
<i>she never works in medicine again!</i>

1013
01:03:51,994 --> 01:03:53,955
Dr. Gye, please. Please wake up!
